Rerun the communication condition (fish, from the main checkout). I kept the budget at 500000, which is what the other arms' logs show:

fish
cd ~/Documents/thesis/slap-mapd-coupling
test -d examples/output; and echo "move examples/output away first"
env PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True \
  ~/.venvs/rl/bin/python examples/04_decentralised_training.py \
  --horizon=630 --arrival-rate=0.15 --env-runners=7 --gpu \
  --budget-env-steps=500000 --eval-seeds=3 --communication \
  2>&1 | tee ~/thesis_runs/run_04_h630_rate0.15_comm_retry.log
mv examples/output ~/thesis_runs/h630_rate0.15_comm_retry

Close the browser or any other GPU-heavy app first, since that frees the roughly 1 GB the crash was short of. If it still runs out of memory, the next step is lowering minibatch_size from 128 (examples/04_decentralised_training.py:242) or dropping --gpu for this one run. I haven't changed either, because minibatch_size is a training hyperparameter. Say if you want it changed.

If you do want to re-evaluate the section checkpoint:

fish
~/.venvs/rl/bin/python examples/04b_evaluate_checkpoint.py \
  --checkpoint=/home/bjarkek/ray_results/section_fixed_only/PPO_warehouse_mapd_multi_agent_env_6170e_00000_0_2026-10-14_11-33-57/checkpoint_000000 \
  --arm=section --eval-seeds=3 --arrival-rate=0.15 --horizon=630

For the communication checkpoint later, use --arm=decentralised --communication, with the same flags otherwise.

